.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt KAIGI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kaigi
.Nd administer the Kaigi conferencing service on FreeBSD
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm service
.Cm kaigi
.Ar start | stop | restart | status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Kaigi is the FreeGateway Project's self-hosted video conferencing service,
derived from MiroTalk SFU and built on mediasoup.
Every participant authenticates and receives access to explicitly authorized
meetings. Browser resources are served locally.
Kaigi uses its own service, configuration, runtime and log directories,
allowing a separate MiroTalk installation to coexist.
.Pp
Kaigi supports self-hosted, open-source, administrator-controlled infrastructure.
Integrations that require third-party-controlled services are not supported.
.Pp
The
.Nm
port installs Kaigi under
.Pa %%WWWDIR%%
and integrates it with the FreeBSD rc system.
Enable it with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kaigi_enable="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
The rc.conf interface is intentionally limited to service
execution:
.Bl -tag -width "kaigi_daemon_group"
.It Va kaigi_enable
Enable the service.  Default:
.Dq NO .
.It Va kaigi_daemon_user
Service user passed to
.Xr daemon 8 .  Default:
.Dq www .
.It Va kaigi_daemon_group
Group used for the service runtime and log directories.  Default:
.Dq www .
.El
.Sh APPLICATION CONFIGURATION
Use
.Xr kaigi.conf 5
for deployment, site, and application environment settings.
The application configuration code at
.Pa %%WWWDIR%%/app/src/config.js
is package-owned and is replaced on upgrades.
Do not edit it to configure the service.
Administrator settings belong in
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf .
Kaigi does not read or migrate settings from a MiroTalk installation.
.Sh SITE ASSETS
Site-owned logos and other presentation files may be stored in
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/site-assets
and are served under
.Pa /site-assets/ .
The administrator-owned
.Pa site.css
is loaded after Kaigi's packaged stylesheets so local CSS can adjust such things
as logo dimensions without patching package-owned CSS.
.Pp
The unauthenticated
.Pa /about
page identifies the site and upstream open-source software and provides the
Corresponding Source link for the exact FreeBSD package revision.
.Sh LOCAL USERS
Local authentication is enabled by default in
.Xr kaigi.conf 5 .
The account database is
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/users
and should be owned by
.Li root:wheel
with mode 0600.
.Pp
Each account occupies one line with four fields separated by
.Ql | :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
username | password | display name | allowed rooms
.Ed
.Pp
Whitespace around fields is ignored.
Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.Ql #
are ignored.
The
.Ql |
character and newline cannot occur in a field.
The allowed-rooms field is either
.Ql *
or a JSON array of exact meeting keys.
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fred    | H7mQ9kR4WxPc | Fred Bloggs | *
mary    | N8vK2pT7YsQa | Mary Smith  | ["staff", "weekly"]
.Ed
.Pp
A template is installed as
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/users.sample .
.Sh JWT SECRET
On first start the rc script creates
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/jwt-secret
from 32 bytes of kernel-provided random data.
The resulting 256-bit secret is root-owned, mode 0600, and reused on later
starts.
Kaigi consumes it during configuration and removes
.Ev JWT_SECRET
from the Node process environment.
.Sh LOGGING
Standard output and error are written to
.Pa /var/log/kaigi/kaigi.log .
The package installs a
.Xr newsyslog 8
configuration to rotate this log rather than retaining it indefinitely.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "%%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf.sample"
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf
Deployment and site configuration.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf.sample
Package-provided deployment example.
.It Pa %%WWWDIR%%/app/src/config.js
Package-owned application configuration code.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/users
Root-only local user database.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/users.sample
Example local user database.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/site-assets
Site-owned presentation assets.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/jwt-secret
Automatically generated JWT signing secret.
.It Pa /var/run/kaigi
Runtime state and pid file.
.It Pa /var/log/kaigi/kaigi.log
Service log.
.El
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Kaigi's security model, administrator choices and audit limits are documented in
.Pa %%DOCSDIR%%/HARDENING.md .
.Pp
The files
.Pa users
and
.Pa jwt-secret
contain secrets and should remain root-owned mode 0600.
.Pp
.Pa kaigi.conf
is read as configuration data by Kaigi and is not executed as shell code.
Do not place user passwords or the JWT secret in it or in
.Pa rc.conf .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kaigi.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr service 8
.Sh PRIVACY
The site administrator defines the deployment's privacy policy.
A site privacy policy link is optional and is configured with
.Va PRIVACY_POLICY_NAME
or
.Va PRIVACY_POLICY_URL
in
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf .
If neither is configured, the user interface does not display a Privacy Policy link.
.Sh SITE COPYRIGHT
Site-specific material may have a different copyright owner from the Kaigi
software and its upstream components.  Set
.Va SITE_COPYRIGHT
in
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/kaigi/kaigi.conf
to display an optional site copyright notice in the login footer and local
About page. Kaigi and upstream software attribution, copyright, license
and Corresponding Source information remain on the About page.
